## [v4.0.0], 2026-11-05
### Migration guide
This release contains breaking changes. Most code only needs the
adaptations below; the entries in the following sections describe all
changes in detail.

Python 3.11 or newer is required.

#### Exceptions
- `rt.exceptions.ConnectionError` was renamed to
  `rt.exceptions.RtConnectionError`. Code catching the builtin `ConnectionError`
  keeps working, as `RtConnectionError` is a subclass of it:
- REST2 raises `rt.exceptions.UnexpectedResponseError` instead of
  `json.JSONDecodeError` for responses which are not valid JSON.
- REST2 raises `rt.exceptions.NotAllowedError` instead of
  `UnexpectedResponseError` if RT answers with HTTP status 403, i.e. if the user
  does not have the rights for a request, and instead of `BadRequestError` if RT
  answers with HTTP status 400 and "Permission Denied" (`tickets.reply()` and
  `tickets.comment()` without the right to add messages).
- REST2 raises `rt.exceptions.InvalidUseError` instead of `ValueError` for
  invalid arguments. `InvalidUseError` is a subclass of `ValueError`, so `except
  ValueError` keeps working.

#### REST1
- Pass all constructor arguments by keyword, as well as `cc`, `bcc`,
  `content_type` and `files` of `reply()`/`comment()`
- *httpx2* replaces *requests*: use the httpx2 authentication classes, and
  `Rt.session` is an `httpx2.Client`
- Credentials in `.netrc` files are no longer used automatically, redirects are
  not followed, requests time out after 20 seconds (`http_timeout=None` disables
  the timeout) and files to attach must be bytes or binary file objects.

#### REST2
- The methods of the REST2 clients are grouped by the kind of object in
  attributes of the client: `tracker.tickets`, `tracker.users`,
  `tracker.groups`, `tracker.queues`, `tracker.assets`, `tracker.catalogs`,
  `tracker.articles`, `tracker.classes`, `tracker.custom_fields`,
  `tracker.custom_roles` and `tracker.rights`. The names lose the name of the
  object, and there are no aliases of the old names. `get_system_info()`,
  `close()`/`aclose()` and the context manager stay on the client.
- The sync `tickets.history()`, `tickets.get_attachments()`,
  `tickets.get_attachments_ids()` and `queues.all()` return iterators instead of
  lists; wrap them in `list()` if a list is needed:
- The async `tickets.new_correspondence()` and `tickets.last_updated()` are
  iterated without `await`:
- `tickets.search()` quotes and escapes all values, so remove any manual
  escaping of quotes in values (`raw_query` is still passed to RT as is).
  Unknown operator suffixes (e.g. `Subject__likee`) raise `InvalidUseError`, and
  a field name containing `__` needs an explicit operator, e.g.
  `CF_my__field__exact='value'`.
- `tickets.reply()` and `tickets.comment()` raise `InvalidUseError` for a
  `content_type` other than `text/plain` or `text/html`.
- `http_auth` and `token` can not be combined anymore.
- Pass all optional arguments by keyword, e.g. `queue` of
  `tickets.search()`/`tickets.last_updated()`, `delete` of
  `tickets.edit_link()`, `privileged` of `users.exists()` and all arguments of
  `assets.search()`. Only `content` of `tickets.reply()`/`tickets.comment()` can
  still be passed by position:
- The parameter `query_format` of `tickets.search()`, `tickets.get()`,
  `assets.get()`, `tickets.get_attachments()` and `assets.search()` was renamed
  to `fields`. A remaining `query_format=` in `tickets.search()` is sent to RT
  as search condition, which RT rejects with `BadRequestError: Unknown field:
  query_format`.
- All methods changing something return an `ActionResult`. Of the methods of
  version 3.8, these returned a `bool` before: `tickets.edit()`,
  `assets.edit()`, `tickets.reply()`, `tickets.comment()`, `tickets.take()`,
  `tickets.untake()`, `tickets.steal()`, `tickets.merge()` and
  `tickets.edit_link()`; `users.edit()` and `queues.edit()` returned the list of
  status messages of RT, which is `result.messages` now (a tuple). RT answers
  with HTTP status 200 and status messages also if it refused all or a part of a
  request (verified with RT 5.0 and 6.0: accepted fields are changed, refused
  ones are reported only as message). The `ActionResult` is **true whenever RT
  executed the request**, so `if tracker.tickets.comment(...)` keeps working,
  but code checking the result with `is True`, or the list of
  `users.edit()`/`queues.edit()` for being empty (nothing changed), must be
  changed: `result.complete`, `result.refused`, `result.unrecognized` and
  `result.messages` give the details, and `result.raise_for_refused()` raises
  `NotFoundError`, `NotAllowedError` or `InvalidUseError` for refused parts. The
  messages are classified with a catalog of the messages of RT
  (`rt/_messages.py`); a message which is not in the catalog (newer RT, other
  language) is listed in `result.unrecognized`. It does not raise for the
  `edit()` methods, `tickets.reply()` and `tickets.comment()`; `tickets.take()`,
  `tickets.untake()`, `tickets.steal()`, `tickets.merge()` and
  `tickets.edit_link()` raise `UnexpectedResponseError` for it, as the message
  is the only information about their result. Refused parts of `tickets.edit()`
  are not raised anymore (before, only a nonexistent user or queue was).
- `rt.common.REGEX_PATTERNS` was removed (not used anymore; the messages of RT
  are recognized by the library itself).
- `tickets.new_correspondence()` only returns tickets last updated by other
  users than the one of the connection, as documented (before, it returned all
  tickets).
- The type aliases `TYPE_VALID_TICKET_LINK_NAMES` and `TYPE_CONTENT_TYPE` were
  renamed to `TicketLinkName` and `ContentType`.
- `Attachment` is immutable; create a modified copy with
  `dataclasses.replace(attachment, file_name='new.txt')`.
- The `base_url` attribute was removed; use
  `tracker.url.removesuffix('REST/2.0/')` if needed.
- The parameter `query_filter` of `tickets.get_attachments()` and
  `tickets.get_attachments_ids()` was renamed to `search_params`, as in all
  other searches. The search conditions no longer replace the condition matching
  only files: pass `files_only=False` to get all parts of the messages (e.g.
  their text), which `query_filter=[]` returned before.
- `tickets.search()` raises `InvalidUseError` if `raw_query` is combined with
  conditions (keyword arguments or `conditions`), which were silently ignored
  before; add them to the query instead. `queue` and `order` can still be
  combined with it.
- `users.exists()` requires `privileged`: before, it defaulted to `True`, so it
  returned `False` for existing unprivileged users (e.g. requestors), which was
  easily overlooked:
- `users.create()` and `users.edit()` accept the fields of users of RT 5.0 and
  6.0: use `NickName` instead of `Nickname` and `FreeformContactInfo` instead of
  `ContactInfo`, which RT ignored. `EmailEncoding`, `WebEncoding`,
  `ExternalContactInfoId`, `ContactInfoSystem`, `ExternalAuthId` and
  `AuthSystem` were removed, as they are no fields of RT 5.0 or newer and RT
  ignored them; `Timezone` and `SMIMECertificate` were added.
- `tickets.history()` and `assets.history()` return the fields `Field`,
  `OldValue`, `NewValue`, `Data` and `TimeTaken` of each transaction instead of
  `Description`, which RT always returned empty.
- `tickets.get_links()` also returns links to URLs (`type` `external`, e.g.
  created with `tickets.edit_link(1, 'RefersTo', url)`), which were missing
  before; filter by `link['type'] == 'ticket'` for the links between tickets
  only.

